        "original_id": "4fb475a3-5528-5add-b1a2-7cb34c7a3b25",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Candy, John Hughes\n- Works: Planes, Trains and Automobiles\n- Roles: Del Griffith\n- Topics: Canadian actors, comedians, Hollywood films\n\nFacts:\n- John Franklin Candy was born on October 31, 1950, and he was a Canadian actor and comedian known mainly for his work in Hollywood films.\n- In 1987, John Hughes wrote, produced, and directed the American comedy film Planes, Trains and Automobiles.\n- John Candy gave one of his most renowned onscreen performances as Del Griffith in the John Hughes comedy Planes, Trains and Automobiles.\n- Del Griffith is portrayed as a loquacious, constantly traveling shower-curtain-ring salesman.\n- John Franklin Candy died on March 4, 1994.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
